## Exact integration contract

Use `profiles/v4` as the explicit import root in a new caller process. Read the
retained run, call `common.frozen_guard(run)` and `evidence.admit_artifacts(run)`,
reconstruct policy/family with `run.policy_and_family(run, candidate)`, and load
the native typed certificate from `results_attempt4/certificate.json`.
`run.trust_for(run)` creates the native verifier against the externally retained
test-only key commitment. A caller must check actual-current-time certificate
admission before dispatch; the audit's historical-time verification is only an
audit of the earlier execution. Do not edit the original certificate's expiry,
bindings or payload. The private test key is outside published evidence.

Construct `runtime.NativeTestRuntime(candidate, certificate, verifier, policy)`.
Its `execute(payload, ordinal)` returns the actual native invocation, execution
and computed decision. Inputs are closed objects with `values` and `budget`:
length zero through six, exact integer budget -1 through 25, values consisting
of integers -2 through 9, booleans, floats 1.25/2.5, or the string `x`. The
decision checks exact integers in 0 through 7 with total at most the budget.
The adapter is bound to the original catalog/source, policy, task, environment
and exact selected IR. It is not a generic source-change or registry-reuse API.
Any original-matrix caller needs its own source/profile freeze, real input and
publication identity joins, actual timing, and applicable lifecycle controls.
